{
  "_comment": [
    "Declarations for the Lodestone census (tools/lodestone_census.py).",
    "",
    "The census enumerates every field in ng2_settings.h itself. This file does",
    "not list subjects - it explains the ones the census cannot verify on its",
    "own, and every entry needs a reason a person can disagree with.",
    "",
    "'reason' declares a setting that is deliberately not in the settings UI.",
    "'doc_phrase' gives the words the public README uses for it, because the",
    "README is written for players and says 'Detail strength', not",
    "'texture_ai_strength'. Without it the census would demand identifiers in",
    "prose, which would make the docs worse to pass a test.",
    "'undocumented_ok' declares a setting that is reachable but is not worth a",
    "line in the README - internal state a player sets by using the app, not by",
    "reading about it."
  ],
  "declared": [
    {
      "setting": "chapter12_workaround",
      "reason": "cvar-only escape hatch (ng2_chapter12_workaround, on the F4 screen). The guard in patch_hooks.cpp makes it unnecessary; it exists only if that guard ever proves too permissive, and putting it in the player-facing menu would advertise a switch that should stay unused."
    },
    {
      "setting": "hardware_detected",
      "reason": "a run-once flag, not a knob. It records that first-run detection has happened so it does not run again; the player re-runs it with the Autodetect button instead.",
      "undocumented_ok": true
    },
